author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 540
acceptance_criteria: "A generated inventory finds every removed or deprecated symbol and classifies source, test, doc, package, and release-probe usage; Canonical 2026-07-28 code and public docs contain no initialize-state, ping, logging/setLevel, roots-change, legacy resource-subscription, session-header, SSE-resume, or tasks/result behavior; Every deprecated feature uses the specification migration path and has a dated compatibility and removal policy; Legacy adapters are isolated from canonical SDK policy and have protocol-era positive and negative tests; CI fails when a removed symbol or deprecated feature is reintroduced outside the explicit adapter allowlist"
goal: No new dependence on removed or deprecated MCP features
objective: "Inventory every legacy feature in source, tests, docs, packages, examples, and release probes and migrate it to the 2026-07-28 path"
value: The current implementation does not carry dead protocol state or teach agents patterns scheduled for removal
why_now: "The latest revision removes ping and several session or subscription behaviors and deprecates Roots, Sampling, Logging, Dynamic Client Registration, HTTP+SSE, and includeContext values"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Migrated and verified
expected_result: "No unclassified canonical dependence on removed or deprecated MCP 2026-07-28 behavior, with every bounded source disposition documented."
actual_result: "Legacy behavior is isolated behind one adapter, all five inventory dispositions are documented, canonical violations are zero, and the CI inventory ratchet passes."
